BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wednesday Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260513T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260513T143000
UID:69b45639a2492930199a12ed@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Share your love of reading at our Wednesday and Thursday Book 
 Clubs! We discuss new books and old favourites in a friendly\, welcoming s
 etting. Ask staff for more details.\nApr 8 - The Women by Kristin Hannah\n
 May 13 - The Kiss Quotient by Helen Hoang\nJune 10 - James by Percival E
 verett\nJuly 8 - My Brilliant Friend by Elena Ferrante\nAug 12 - The Sound
  of Gravel by Ruth Wariner\nSept 9 - A House Without Windows by Nadia Hash
 imi\nOct 14 - Tomorrow and Tomorrow and Tomorrow by Gabrielle Zevin\nNov 1
 1 - The Betrayal of Anne Frank by Rosemary Sullivan\nDec 9 - How to Solve 
 Your Own Murder by Kristen Perrin
LOCATION:Eglinton Square\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b45639a2492930199a12ed
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
